<title>PERU: Peru clamps down on nepotism in government.</title>
<headline>Peru clamps down on nepotism in government.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Congress passed a bill on Tuesday aimed at reducing the ability of some public officials to place relatives in government jobs.</p>
<p>&quot;A public official who has the power to hire personnel will no longer be able to use it to employ relatives,&quot; said Jose Arostegui, adviser to the Congressional Labour Committee that drew up the bill.</p>
<p>Nepotism is a common problem in Latin America, where even presidents are frequently accused of giving jobs to family members over better candidates.</p>
</text>
